// std remembers each executable's directories in a buffer of its own: a build that gives
// more can't call declarations, and one that doesn't call it is fine.
// `ctxc graph` runs the build program without building the executables, whose files needn't
// compile. ctxc's own directory for it is removed before and after: the runner clears those of
// `ctxc run` commands only.
//# remove {work:.}
//# $ ctxc graph . {dir}/graph-gen {dir}/graph.txt
//# exit: 1
//# stderr:
//| build: panic: build: too many directories for build::declarations to remember
//|   at build::declarations(arena::Arena) ({home}/std/build/declarations.ctx:{n}:{n})
//|   at build (build.ctx:11:48)
//# remove {work:.}
